    <main id="main-content" class="static-main">
      <article class="px-5 pt-12 pb-6 lg:px-8 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-16 max-w-[1600px] mx-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-brand-200 uppercase tracking-wide">Chapter 4</span>
          <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-500/30 to-transparent"></span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="section-title text-3xl tracking-tight leading-tight lg:text-5xl">Blocks and Chains</h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] lg:mt-4 lg:text-xl text-brand-200">Linking blocks together with cryptographic link hashes</p>

        <section class="mt-8 lg:mt-12 reveal" id="introduction">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Introduction</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              Imagine a set of Lego bricks. Each brick can hold information — names, numbers, dates. Now imagine that each brick is glued to the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">previous</span> brick using a special, unbreakable glue. If you try to swap out a brick in the middle, the glue would break, and you would know something is wrong. That is exactly how blocks and chains work in a blockchain.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              Blocks are packets of transaction records, while the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">Chain</span> is the cryptographic sequence linking each block to the hash of the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">previous</span> one. Together, they create a permanent, verifiable history.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              In this chapter, you will learn what goes inside a block, how blocks are connected to form a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span>, and why this structure makes blockchain data so trustworthy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="how-it-works">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">How It Works</h2>

            <div class="mt-4 p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Blocks are containers that hold a batch of valid transactions. Each block has a header (containing metadata like the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">previous</span> block's hash, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('timestamp')">timestamp</span>, and <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span>) and a body (the list of transactions). The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span> is formed by each block referencing the hash of the block before it.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-5 p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-3">Everyday Object Analogy</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Think of a blockchain like a train. Each train car is a block filled with cargo (transactions). Each car is locked to the car in front of it using a unique coupling (hash). If someone tries to swap out a car in the middle, the couplings would not match, and the whole train would fall apart.</p>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">Anatomy of a Block</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              Every block has two main parts:
            </p>
            <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M4 6h16M4 10h16M4 14h16M4 18h16"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200"><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('block-header')">Block Header</span></h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Contains the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">previous</span> block's hash, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('timestamp')">timestamp</span>, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span>, and the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('merkle-root')">Merkle root</span> of all transactions.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">Block Body</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Contains the actual list of validated transactions included in this block.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">How Blocks Are Connected</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span> structure ensures integrity:
            </p>
            <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-1">Step 1</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Block N is created. Its hash is computed from its contents and stored in Block N+1.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-1">Step 2</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Block N+1 includes the hash of Block N in its own header, creating a link.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-1">Step 3</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">If Block N is tampered with, its hash changes, breaking the link with N+1.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">Deeper Dive</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              The strength of a blockchain comes from this hash-based linking. To alter a single transaction in Block 2, an attacker would need to recalculate the hash of Block 2, Block 3, Block 4, and every subsequent block — all before the rest of the network adds new blocks. This becomes exponentially harder as the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span> grows longer.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              In Bitcoin, the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('block-header')">block header</span> contains a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('merkle-root')">Merkle root</span> — a single hash that represents all transactions in the block. This allows anyone to verify that a transaction is included in a block without downloading the entire block's data.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-5 p-4 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-2">Key Insight</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The term "blockchain" comes from exactly this structure: blocks of data chained together by cryptographic hashes. Without the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span>, each block would be an isolated, untrusted data packet.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="vocabulary">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Vocabulary Table</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="vocab-table w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th class="text-theme">Term</th>
                    <th class="text-theme">Definition</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="text-theme-muted">
                  <tr id="vocab-block-header"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('block-header')">Block Header</span></td><td>The part of a block containing metadata: previous hash, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('timestamp')">timestamp</span>, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span>, and <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('merkle-root')">Merkle root</span>.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-merkle-root"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('merkle-root')">Merkle Root</span></td><td>A single hash representing all transactions in a block, used for efficient verification.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-previous-hash"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">Previous Hash</span></td><td>The cryptographic hash of the preceding block, linking blocks together.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-timestamp"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('timestamp')">Timestamp</span></td><td>A digital label indicating when a block was created.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-nonce"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">Nonce</span></td><td>A number miners adjust to produce a hash meeting the network's difficulty target.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-chain"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">Chain</span></td><td>The sequence of blocks linked by cryptographic hashes from the genesis block to the latest.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-block-height"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('block-height')">Block Height</span></td><td>The number of blocks preceding a given block in the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span>.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-orphan-block"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('orphan-block')">Orphan Block</span></td><td>A valid block that is not part of the main <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span> because another block was accepted first.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="fun-facts">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Fun Facts</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The Bitcoin blockchain's genesis block (Block 0) was mined on January 3, 2009, and contains a hidden newspaper headline.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">A Bitcoin block can hold between 1,500 and 2,000 transactions on average, depending on transaction size.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The Merkle tree structure in a block allows you to verify a single transaction's inclusion using only a few hashes, not the whole block.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">If all the blocks in Bitcoin were stacked on top of each other, the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span> would be over 500 GB of data.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The term "blockchain" was actually popularized by Bitcoin — the original 2008 whitepaper never uses the word, instead calling it a "<span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span> of blocks."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Interactive Diagram -->
        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="interactive-diagram">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8 text-center">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Interactive Diagram</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-theme-muted">Launch the interactive diagram to see this in action.</p>
            <a href="diagrams/diagram-04-introduction-blockch/index.html" class="btn-primary magnetic-btn inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm py-3 px-6 mt-4" aria-label="Open interactive diagram">
              Open Interactive Diagram
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="knowledge-check">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Knowledge Check</h2>

            <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">

              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">1. What piece of data links one block to the next in a blockchain?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span></label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">previous</span> block's hash</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The block number</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('timestamp')">timestamp</span></label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('previous-hash')">previous</span> block's hash</p>
              </div>

              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">2. What is a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('merkle-root')">Merkle root</span> used for?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> To encrypt transactions</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> To summarize all transactions in a block for efficient verification</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> To find the next block's <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span></label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> To identify the sender of a transaction</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> To summarize all transactions in a block for efficient verification</p>
              </div>

              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">3. What happens if an attacker tries to edit the data in Block 2 of a 100-block <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('chain')">chain</span>?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> Only Block 2's hash changes</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> Block 2 and all subsequent blocks become invalid</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> The blockchain automatically repairs itself</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> The attacker needs only to fix Block 2's hash</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Block 2 and all subsequent blocks become invalid</p>
              </div>

            </div>

            <div class="mt-6 text-center">
              <button type="button" id="reveal-answers-btn" class="btn-primary magnetic-btn text-sm py-2.5 px-6">Show Answers</button>
            </div>

            <script>
              (function() {
                var btn = document.getElementById('reveal-answers-btn');
                if (btn) {
                  btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
                    var answers = document.querySelectorAll('.kb-answer');
                    var hidden = false;
                    answers.forEach(function(a) {
                      if (!a.classList.contains('revealed')) hidden = true;
                    });
                    answers.forEach(function(a) {
                      a.classList.toggle('revealed', hidden);
                    });
                    btn.textContent = hidden ? 'Hide Answers' : 'Show Answers';
                  });
                }
              })();
            </script>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-12 lg:mt-20 reveal">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-theme-faint text-center mb-4">Chapter Navigation</p>
